x_comment(x_KensicoReservoir,"A #$BalancingReservoir in the #$NewYorkCityWaterSupply system to which water from all three of the #$NewYorkCityWaterSupply reservoir system subsystems (the #$CrotonReservoirSystem, the #$CatskillReservoirSystem, and the #$DelawareReservoirSystem) converge to be piped into New York City.  The majority of the inflow comes from the #$CatskillAqueduct and the #$DelawareAqueduct.  The aqueduct operations can affect the reservoir by bypassing it, flowing through it, or, in the case of the #$CatskillAqueduct, entering \"float\" status, where water can flow either direction at the influent.  Catskill and Delaware water supplies are held in the Kensico Reservoir for approximately 15 to 25 days before proceeding to the New York City distribution system, allowing for impurities to settle.") :- x_cid(a65b1277cbc0c3).
